# zwanzig: Zig 0.17.0 frontend port.
# Base: 1a0768ccd889d3586ec9482f02ffffe872a99749 plus 0001 through 0007.
# Authored 2026-10-31. The embedded frontend is the compiler that builds zwanzig,
# so code using 0.17-only builtins (@backingInt) failed AstGen under the 0.16 build.
# Build with Zig 0.17.0 only: compat.zig now accepts 0.17.0 alone, because the
# port drops AST/ZIR tags 0.17 removed (array_mult, c_import, defer_err_code) and
# reads `errdefer expr` as 0.17 parses it (no payload). DeclContents.explicit_types
# is type_decls; Ast.parse takes options; ** becomes @splat or a comptime repeat;
# std.meta.fields/bufPrintZ/b.args/zon.parse follow their 0.17 replacements.
# Tests: fixture_tests.zig adopts prepareProject (0001-0007 changed that API without
# it); the two errdefer-payload fixtures are removed (the syntax no longer exists);
# a no-resize backing allocator keeps two allocation-failure sweeps deterministic
# under 0.17's SafeAllocator. 711/728 tests pass; the 17 failures are the ones the
# 0001-0007 tree already has under Zig 0.16.0. No rule or severity changes.
# Apply after 0007 with: git apply -p1 <this file>
